// A planted EXPLANATORY chain (26 Sep 2026): no intervention, a condition it sets out from,
// a state that is both where the circle starts and what it explains (Merton's prejudice), a
// reflexive loop the text closes, and a declared condition the text links to nothing.
===
title: "Loop -- a planted explanatory chain"
mechanism:
    question: "How does worry sustain itself?"
    levels: [macro, meso, micro]
    actors:
        person: {label: "The worrier", level: micro}
    states:
        worry:  {label: "Worry", actor: person, role: [condition, outcome]}
        check:  {label: "Checking", actor: person}
        relief: {label: "Momentary relief", actor: person, role: outcome}
        habit:  {label: "A habit of worry", actor: person, role: condition}
===

[Worry sustains itself]: Worry sustains itself through the checking it prompts.

[Worry drives checking]: Worry drives checking.
    {causes: {from: worry, to: check, sign: "+", basis: asserted}}
    +> [Worry sustains itself]

[Checking feeds worry]: Checking, by treating the danger as real, feeds the worry.
    {causes: {from: check, to: worry, sign: "+", basis: asserted, reflexive: true}}
    +> [Worry sustains itself]

[Checking brings relief]: Checking brings a moment of relief.
    {causes: {from: check, to: relief, sign: "+", basis: asserted}}
    +> [Worry sustains itself]
